From: axon7m bring-up
Subject: [PATCH] android: use the platform's libcamera_metadata

The vendored camera_metadata copy validates against an older tag table and
aborted the camera provider on Android 17's request settings
(append_camera_metadata: assertion "validate_camera_metadata_structure(dst,
NULL) == OK" failed, from Camera3RequestDescriptor). Link against the
platform library (LLNDK, used by the provider too) through a stub with the
same soname, as the NDK has no libcamera_metadata.
---
--- a/src/android/meson.build
+++ b/src/android/meson.build
@@ -45,10 +45,14 @@
     'metadata/camera_metadata.c',
 ])
 
-android_camera_metadata = static_library('camera_metadata',
-                                         android_camera_metadata_sources,
-                                         c_args : '-Wno-shadow',
-                                         include_directories : android_includes)
+# axon7m: use the platform's libcamera_metadata (LLNDK) like the camera
+# provider does. The vendored copy validates against an older tag table and
+# aborted on Android 17's request settings (append_camera_metadata:
+# validate_camera_metadata_structure failed). The NDK has no such library, so
+# link against a stub with the same soname; the real one is loaded at run time.
+android_camera_metadata = shared_library('camera_metadata',
+                                         files('metadata/camera_metadata_stub.c'),
+                                         install : false)
 
 libcamera_hal = shared_library('libcamera-hal',
                                android_hal_sources,
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/android/metadata/camera_metadata_stub.c
@@ -0,0 +1,51 @@
